    "problemStatement": "Nayra doesn't like stories of people receiving random trees as birthday presents, but this time she received a tree as a present for her own birthday! After struggling for a day trying to figure out what to do with this tree, she asked Aryan for help. He gave her this problem.\n\nYou are given a tree with NNN vertices and weighted edges. It is rooted at vertex 111.\n\nDefine g(u,v)g(u,v)g(u,v) to be the maximum weight of an edge on the shortest path between vertex uuu and vertex vvv in this tree.\n\nJust calculating g(u,v)g(u,v)g(u,v) is too easy, so you have to process QQQ queries.\n\nIn each query, you are given KKK **distinct** vertices v1,v2,…,vKv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_Kv1​,v2​,…,vK​. You have to compute the sum of the ggg-values of each pair of vertices among these KKK, i.e, the value\n\n∑i=1K−1∑j=i+1Kg(vi,vj)\\sum_{i=1}^{K-1} \\sum_{j=i+1}^K g(v_i, v_j)∑i=1K−1​∑j=i+1K​g(vi​,vj​)\n\n**Note**: The input and output are large, so use fast input-output methods.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ, denoting the number of vertices in the tree and the number of queries respectively.\nThe second line contains N−1N-1N−1 space-separated integers P2,P3,…,PNP_2, P_3, \\dots, P_NP2​,P3​,…,PN​, where PiP_iPi​ is the parent of vertex iii.\nThe third line contains N−1N-1N−1 space-separated integers W2,W3,…,WNW_2, W_3, \\dots, W_NW2​,W3​,…,WN​, where WiW_iWi​ is the weight of the edge between vertices iii and PiP_iPi​.\nThe next QQQ lines contain queries you will have to answer. The description of QQQ queries follows.\nThe iii-th line contains an integer KiK_iKi​ followed by KiK_iKi​ distinct space-separated integers v1,v2,…,vKiv_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_{K_i}v1​,v2​,…,vKi​​, where KiK_iKi​ is the number of vertices in this query and v1,v2,…vKiv_1, v_2, \\ldots v_{K_i}v1​,v2​,…vKi​​ denote the vertices themselves.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test, print one line containing QQQ space-separated integers. The iii-th of these integers should be the answer to the iii-th query.",
